6. SWING / TREND STARTS
============================================================
[ ] 1PM start
      1PMX DT Resistance @ <level>   // ALWAYS name the level that acted as resistance (latest first-touch group, e.g. 1E100, 1E50, 1E200)
      1PMX UT Support @ <level>      // ALWAYS name the level that acted as support (latest first-touch group, e.g. S1 D, Daily VWAP, 5E100)
      // 1PMX DT fires on the FIRST bar where 1m PVT < 0 AND 1m MACD2 is
      //   downtrending hold together after an Uptrend state — same bar or a
      //   few bars apart (stateful pair alignment, 2026-11-10 rule).
      //   UT mirrors it: PVT > 0 AND MACD2 uptrending after a Downtrend state.

[ ] 1PM E50 follow-through (2026-11-10, v2026-11-10.42)
      Attention: 1PME50 UT Started Support @ <levels>   // after a 1PM uptrend start, the FIRST price cross above 1E50
      Attention: 1PME50 DT Started Resistance @ <levels> // after a 1PM downtrend start, the FIRST price cross below 1E50
      // once per trend episode (re-armed by each new 1PMX start)
      // 5PM starts keep their wording: "5PM Uptrend started.." / "5PM Downtrend started.."

[ ] 1PM E50 swing start
      1PME50 downswing has started.. Nearby levels are <Levels> in the vicinity of 100 points below
      1PME50 upswing has started.. Nearby levels are <Levels> in the vicinity of 100 points above
      But 5m PVT is still at <val>..Watch out.. // This announcement has to be made if 5m PVT far above zero line when 1PME50 downswings..and far below zero line when upswing starts..

[ ] Expect pre-call (5m PVT trending, point-in-time) — said ONLY when 1m PVT is
    trending into the level (swing Down only if 1m PVT is uptrending and price
    faces resistance; swing Up only if 1m PVT is downtrending and price takes
    support; never when 1m PVT already trends the same way) AND 1m PVT is
    within the +/-0.1 zero-line threshold — outside the band, don't say it.
      Expect 1PX_15PM DT
      Expect 1PX_15PM UT

